WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:08.027
During causal language-model training, the model learns to predict the token that actually comes next.

00:00:08.027 --> 00:00:14.402
In the example, the model gives forty-eight percent probability to “today,” twenty-four percent to “before,” thirteen

00:00:14.402 --> 00:00:22.902
percent to “and,” eight percent to “late,” five percent to “yesterday,” and the remaining two percent to all other

00:00:22.902 --> 00:00:30.246
vocabulary tokens. The numbers are illustrative, but they now form a complete probability distribution.

00:00:30.805 --> 00:00:34.842
The training target is the word that truly occurs next.

00:00:34.842 --> 00:00:42.027
Training changes the model parameters so that useful next-token probabilities become more likely across enormous numbers

00:00:42.027 --> 00:00:43.366
of examples.
